   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "It adds that, I mesmo that",
   "texto": [
    "**Ainda que** and **mesmo que** (although) usually go with the present conjunctive do: **Ainda que chova, vou à praia** (although it rains, I go to the beach). **Mesmo que digas que não, venho** (even if you say no, I'm going)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Quando and be with future value",
   "texto": [
    "For any future action, use the future of conjunctive after **quando** and **se**: **Quando chegares, avisa-me** (when you arrive, let me know); **Se chover amanhã, ficamos em casa** (if it rains tomorrow, we stay at home). Do not confuse **quando chegas** (when you usually arrive) with **quando chegares** (when you arrive in the future)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Forms of the Conjunctive Future",
   "texto": [
    "In regular verbs, part of the **eles** form of the perfeite preterito and remove **-am**: **falaram → falar**, **comeram → comer**, **partiram → partir**. The resulting form serves **eu/ele/ela/você**; adds **-es** for **tu**, **-mos** for **nós** and **-em** for **eles/elas/vocês**: **quando falar**, **falares**, **falarmos**, **falarem**.",
    "Common irregular forms: **for** (be / go), **tiver**, **fizer**, **vier**, **puder**, **quiser**."
   ]
